module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.AffineHom
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.QuasicoherentPullbackScheme
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.AssociatedModuleFunctor

/-!
# Faithfulness of the associated-module functor on a site of schemes

Tag 03DU attaches to a quasi-coherent module `M` on a scheme `S` a presheaf of modules `Mᵃ` on a
site `C` of schemes over `S`, and
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.AssociatedModuleFunctor` makes that construction
functorial.  Descent, Lemma 0GN7 asserts that `M ↦ Mᵃ` is *fully faithful* on quasi-coherent
modules, for each of the five topologies and for both the big and the small site.  This file
proves the **faithful** half over an affine base, and records why the statement needs a
hypothesis on the site at all.

Both parts answer the same question — how much of `φ : M ⟶ N` can be read off the maps
`Γ(T, T.hom⁺ M) → Γ(T, T.hom⁺ N)` indexed by the objects `T` of the site?  The answer is: the
whole of `φ` as soon as one object of the site is `S` itself and `S` is affine, because then one
of those maps *is* `Γ(S, φ)`, and on an affine scheme a morphism of quasi-coherent modules is its
map on global sections (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.hom_ext_of_app_top`).  And nothing
at all if the site is empty, in which case there are no maps to read.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hom_ext_of_pullback_app_top`: over an affine scheme, a
  morphism of quasi-coherent modules is determined by the global sections of its pullback along
  an isomorphism.
* `Stacks.Sites.associatedModuleMap_injective`: **the faithfulness half of Descent, Lemma 0GN7
  over an affine base.**  If `S` is affine and some object `X₀` of the site has invertible
  structure morphism to `S`, then `φ ↦ Stacks.Sites.associatedModuleMap S toOver φ` is
  injective.
* `Stacks.Sites.faithful_associatedModuleFunctor` and
  `Stacks.Sites.faithful_associatedSheafFunctor`: the same statement as faithfulness of the
  functors `Stacks.Sites.associatedModuleFunctor` and `Stacks.Sites.associatedSheafFunctor`.
* `Stacks.Sites.subsingleton_hom_associatedModulePresheaf_of_isEmpty` and
  `Stacks.Sites.not_bijective_associatedModuleMap_of_isEmpty`: over an empty site every two
  morphisms of associated presheaves of modules are equal, so `φ ↦ Mᵃ ⟶ Nᵃ` is not injective as
  soon as `M` and `N` have two distinct morphisms.
* `Stacks.Sites.exists_ne_hom_tilde_unit` and
  `Stacks.Sites.not_bijective_associatedModuleMap_emptyFullSubcategory`: an instance of the
  previous item with every parameter supplied — the associated sheaf of `R` over `Spec R` for a
  nontrivial ring `R`, and the empty full subcategory of `Over (Spec R)`.

## Implementation notes

The hypothesis on the site is `IsIso (toOver.obj X₀).hom` rather than an isomorphism
`toOver.obj X₀ ≅ Over.mk (𝟙 S)` in `Over S`: the two are interchangeable, and the first is what
instance search can discharge at a use site.  On the slice of a small étale site at a chart `X`
the object `CategoryTheory.Over.mk (𝟙 X)` satisfies it, since the projection to the schemes over
the chart's scheme is `CategoryTheory.Over.post` of a functor and therefore sends the identity to
the identity.

The component of `Stacks.Sites.associatedModuleMap` at an object is the map on global sections of
the pullback *definitionally but not syntactically*: the two carry different spellings of the
same module of sections, so the equality of the components cannot be stated as an equality of
morphisms and `Stacks.Sites.associatedModuleMap_app_apply` is elementwise.  Accordingly the
faithfulness proof moves to elements with `congrArg` at a binder whose type is written out; a
`rw` with that lemma reaches the goal but the subsequent rewrite with the hypothesis fails its
motive check.

`Stacks.Sites.not_bijective_associatedModuleMap_of_isEmpty` is the reason the main result carries
a hypothesis on the site.  It is not a defect of Tag 0GN7, whose five sites all contain `S`; it is
a defect of any formulation of 0GN7 that quantifies over an arbitrary `toOver : C ⥤ Over S`.  A
second restriction is also necessary and is not formalized here: over a base that is *not* affine,
knowing `Γ(S, φ)` alone does not determine `φ`, so the hypothesis `IsAffine S` cannot simply be
dropped in favour of the presence of `X₀` — the site has to be large enough to see an affine
covering of `S`, which is how the source's own proof proceeds.

**What is not proved here.**  Fullness.  Reading a morphism `a : Mᵃ ⟶ Nᵃ` as some `φᵃ` needs its
component at `X₀` *plus* the identification of the component at an arbitrary object `T` of the
site, and that identification is not a formal consequence of naturality: the `Γ(T, 𝒪)`-module
`Γ(T, T.hom⁺ M)` is in general not generated by the image of `Γ(S, M)`, so two `Γ(T, 𝒪)`-linear
maps agreeing on that image can differ.  The source instead identifies the two over the *affine*
objects of the site, where the comparison is the base change of
`AlgebraicGeometry.pullbackTildeIso`, and then propagates the identification by the sheaf
condition, the affine objects being a dense subsite.  No `@[stacks]` attribute is therefore
claimed: besides fullness, Tag 0GN7 is stated for an arbitrary base scheme, and this is one
implication over an affine one.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GN7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GN7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01I9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01I9)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

/-- **On an affine scheme a morphism of quasi-coherent modules is its map on global sections,
read after an invertible base change.**  If `g : T ⟶ S` is an isomorphism of schemes with `S`
affine, two morphisms of quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-modules whose pullbacks along `g` agree on global
sections are equal.

Pullback along an isomorphism is faithful, and on the affine scheme `T` a morphism of
quasi-coherent modules is determined by its global sections
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.hom_ext_of_app_top`); the pullbacks are quasi-coherent by
`Stacks.Modules.isQuasicoherent_pullback`. -/
public theorem hom_ext_of_pullback_app_top {T S : Scheme.{u}} (g : T ⟶ S) [IsIso g] [IsAffine S]
    {M N : S.Modules} [M.IsQuasicoherent] [N.IsQuasicoherent] {φ ψ : M ⟶ N}
    (h : ∀ m, ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).map φ).app ⊤ m =
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).map ψ).app ⊤ m) : φ = ψ :=
  have : IsAffine T := IsAffine.of_isIso g
  Functor.map_injective (Scheme.Modules.pullback g)
    (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.hom_ext_of_app_top h)

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

namespace Stacks.Sites

open _root_.AlgebraicGeometry

variable (S : Scheme.{u}) {C : Type (u + 1)} [Category.{u} C] (toOver : C ⥤ Over S)

/-! ### Faithfulness over an affine base -/

section Faithful

variable [IsAffine S] {M N : S.Modules} [M.IsQuasicoherent] [N.IsQuasicoherent]

/-- **The faithfulness half of Descent, Lemma 0GN7 over an affine base.**  Let `S` be an affine
scheme and let `toOver : C ⥤ Over S` present a category of schemes over `S` which contains an
object `X₀` whose structure morphism to `S` is invertible — for the five sites of Tag 0GN7 this
is `S` itself.  Then a morphism of quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-modules is determined by the induced
maps on the sections of the associated presheaves of modules.

The component at `X₀` is the map on global sections of the pullback along an isomorphism, which
determines the morphism by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hom_ext_of_pullback_app_top`; no other object of the site is
used. -/
public theorem associatedModuleMap_injective (X₀ : C) [IsIso (toOver.obj X₀).hom] :
    Function.Injective fun φ : M ⟶ N => associatedModuleMap S toOver φ := by
  intro φ ψ h
  have h' : associatedModuleMap S toOver φ = associatedModuleMap S toOver ψ := h
  refine Scheme.Modules.hom_ext_of_pullback_app_top (toOver.obj X₀).hom (fun m => ?_)
  exact congrArg (fun a : associatedModulePresheaf S M toOver ⟶
    associatedModulePresheaf S N toOver => (a.app (op X₀)).hom m) h'

end Faithful

/-- **Descent, Lemma 0GN7 over an affine base, faithfulness clause, as a property of the
functor.**  The functor `M ↦ Mᵃ` from the quasi-coherent modules on an affine scheme `S` to the
presheaves of modules over the structure presheaf of a site of schemes over `S` containing an
object with invertible structure morphism is faithful. -/
public theorem faithful_associatedModuleFunctor [IsAffine S] (X₀ : C)
    [IsIso (toOver.obj X₀).hom] : (associatedModuleFunctor S toOver).Faithful := by
  constructor
  intro F G φ ψ h
  have := F.property
  have := G.property
  exact ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (associatedModuleMap_injective S toOver X₀ h)

/-- **Descent, Lemma 0GN7 over an affine base, faithfulness clause, at the level of sheaves of
modules.**  Granted the two sheaf conditions that `Stacks.Sites.associatedSheafFunctor` takes as
parameters, that functor is faithful under the same hypotheses on `S` and on the site.  A
morphism of sheaves of modules is its underlying morphism of presheaves of modules, so this is
`Stacks.Sites.faithful_associatedModuleFunctor`. -/
public theorem faithful_associatedSheafFunctor [IsAffine S] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    (hR : Presheaf.IsSheaf J (structurePresheaf S toOver))
    (hM : ∀ (M : S.Modules) (_ : M.IsQuasicoherent),
      Presheaf.IsSheaf J (associatedPresheaf S M toOver))
    (X₀ : C) [IsIso (toOver.obj X₀).hom] :
    (associatedSheafFunctor S toOver J hR hM).Faithful := by
  have := faithful_associatedModuleFunctor S toOver X₀
  constructor
  intro F G φ ψ h
  exact Functor.map_injective (associatedModuleFunctor S toOver)
    (congrArg SheafOfModules.Hom.val h)

/-! ### Why the site needs a hypothesis -/

/-- **Over an empty site there is only one morphism of associated presheaves of modules.**  A
morphism of presheaves of modules is a family of maps indexed by the objects of the site, and
there are none. -/
public theorem subsingleton_hom_associatedModulePresheaf_of_isEmpty [IsEmpty C] (M N : S.Modules)
    [M.IsQuasicoherent] [N.IsQuasicoherent] :
    Subsingleton (associatedModulePresheaf S M toOver ⟶ associatedModulePresheaf S N toOver) := by
  constructor
  intro a b
  refine PresheafOfModules.Hom.ext ?_
  ext X x
  exact isEmptyElim X.unop

/-- **The associated-module construction is not faithful over an empty site.**  If `M` and `N`
have two distinct morphisms then `φ ↦ Mᵃ ⟶ Nᵃ` is not injective, because its target has only
one element.

This is what forces a hypothesis on the site in
`Stacks.Sites.associatedModuleMap_injective`: with no constraint on `toOver : C ⥤ Over S` the
full-faithfulness assertion of Descent, Lemma 0GN7 is false. -/
public theorem not_bijective_associatedModuleMap_of_isEmpty [IsEmpty C] (M N : S.Modules)
    [M.IsQuasicoherent] [N.IsQuasicoherent] (hne : ∃ φ ψ : M ⟶ N, φ ≠ ψ) :
    ¬ Function.Bijective fun φ : M ⟶ N => associatedModuleMap S toOver φ := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨φ, ψ, hφψ⟩ := hne
  have := subsingleton_hom_associatedModulePresheaf_of_isEmpty S toOver M N
  exact hφψ (h.1 (Subsingleton.elim _ _))

/-- **The associated sheaf of a nontrivial ring over its own spectrum has two distinct
endomorphisms.**  The images under `AlgebraicGeometry.tilde.functor` of `0` and of the identity
of `R` as an `R`-module are distinct, that functor being faithful. -/
public theorem exists_ne_hom_tilde_unit (R : CommRingCat.{u}) [Nontrivial R] :
    ∃ φ ψ : (tilde.functor R).obj (ModuleCat.of R R) ⟶ (tilde.functor R).obj (ModuleCat.of R R),
      φ ≠ ψ := by
  refine ⟨(tilde.functor R).map 0, (tilde.functor R).map (𝟙 _), fun h => ?_⟩
  have h0 : (0 : ModuleCat.of R R ⟶ ModuleCat.of R R) = 𝟙 _ :=
    (tilde.functor R).map_injective h
  have h1 := congrArg (fun k : ModuleCat.of R R ⟶ ModuleCat.of R R => k.hom (1 : R)) h0
  simp at h1

/-- **An instance of the failure with every parameter supplied.**  Take the base to be the
spectrum of a nontrivial ring `R`, the module to be the associated sheaf of `R` itself, and the
site to be the empty full subcategory of the schemes over `Spec R`.  Then the map of Descent,
Lemma 0GN7 is not bijective.

So the statement of 0GN7 cannot be formalized by quantifying over an arbitrary functor
`C ⥤ Over S`; the only inhabitant of `Nontrivial` needed here is a nontrivial commutative ring,
for instance `CommRingCat.of (ULift ℤ)`. -/
public theorem not_bijective_associatedModuleMap_emptyFullSubcategory (R : CommRingCat.{u})
    [Nontrivial R] :
    ¬ Function.Bijective fun φ : (tilde.functor R).obj (ModuleCat.of R R) ⟶
        (tilde.functor R).obj (ModuleCat.of R R) =>
      associatedModuleMap (Spec R)
        (ObjectProperty.ι (C := Over (Spec R)) fun _ => False) φ :=
  have : IsEmpty (ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory (C := Over (Spec R)) fun _ => False) :=
    ⟨fun X => X.property⟩
  not_bijective_associatedModuleMap_of_isEmpty (Spec R) _ _ _ (exists_ne_hom_tilde_unit R)

end Stacks.Sites

end
